* OPA1678 AC-analysis model for ngspice/KiCad
* Purpose: stable small-signal AC analysis of the SC440 preamp.
* It is NOT a vendor macro-model and is not intended for clipping/noise/transient validation.
* Parameters based on OPA1678 typical datasheet figures used in this project:
*   Aol = 114 dB = 501187 V/V
*   GBW = 16 MHz
* Dominant pole ~= GBW/Aol = 31.924 Hz
* With RDOM=501187 ohm and CDOM=9.94718 nF, fp ~=31.924 Hz.
* Pin order: IN+ IN- VCC VEE OUT

.SUBCKT OPA1678_AC INP INM VCC VEE OUT
* Input resistance.
RIN INP INM 10T
* Dominant-pole open-loop stage. Current is injected into NDOM for INP>INM.
GOL 0 NDOM INP INM 1
RDOM NDOM 0 501187.2336
CDOM NDOM 0 9.94718394n
* Low-impedance output buffer; 10 ohm open-loop output resistance.
EOUT NBUF 0 NDOM 0 1
ROUT NBUF OUT 10
* Tiny supply-reference paths prevent floating supply pins without loading them.
RVCC VCC 0 1T
RVEE VEE 0 1T
.ENDS OPA1678_AC
